<img src="https://images.code.org/aa8f9680252d49813eb31db8eec9480b-image-1790622861620.png" alt="Microsoft Certified: Azure AI Fundamentals digital badge" style="width: 180px; border-radius: 10px; margin: 0 10px 10px 16px; float: right;">

# Meet AI-901

AI Foundations Year 2 is built toward **Microsoft Certified: Azure AI Fundamentals**, earned by passing the AI-901 exam. Understanding how that exam is structured will help you decide where to spend extra time and attention as you teach.

## The Two-Domain Split

AI-901 has two domains:

<div role="img" aria-label="Bar showing exam weight split: Domain 1, Identify AI concepts and capabilities, 40 to 45 percent, and Domain 2, Implement AI solutions using Microsoft Foundry, 55 to 60 percent" style="display: flex; width: 100%; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">
  <div style="width: 42%; background: #0099F3; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 16px 12px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Domain 1</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px;">40&ndash;45%</div>
  </div>
  <div style="width: 58%; background: #06338D; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 16px 12px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Domain 2</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px;">55&ndash;60%</div>
  </div>
</div>

<table style="width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="background-color: #0099F3;">
      <th scope="col" style="width: 30%; padding: 12px; text-align: left; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 18px;">Domain</th>
      <th scope="col" style="width: 48%; padding: 12px; text-align: left; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 18px;">What it covers</th>
      <th scope="col" style="width: 22%; padding: 12px; text-align: left; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 18px;">Where it lives in the year</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="background-color: #FFFFFF;">
      <th scope="row" style="padding: 12px; text-align: left; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5EFFF; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">Domain 1: Identify AI concepts and capabilities</th>
      <td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5EFFF; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom: 6px;">&bull; Conceptual understanding of AI</div>
        <div style="margin-bottom: 6px;">&bull; Responsible AI principles</div>
        <div>&bull; No implementation required</div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5EFFF; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">Threaded across the full year, in both semesters</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #D5EFFF;">
      <th scope="row" style="padding: 12px; text-align: left; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">Domain 2: Implement AI solutions using Microsoft Foundry</th>
      <td style="padding: 12px; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom: 6px;">&bull; Hands-on deployment and prompting</div>
        <div style="margin-bottom: 6px;">&bull; Building with Foundry</div>
        <div>&bull; Assumes basic Python</div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding: 12px; vertical-align: top; font-size: 16px;">Concentrated in Semester 2 only (Units 7&ndash;10)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div style="background-color: #D5EFFF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #06338D; line-height: 1.5;">
    <strong>Why this matters for how you teach:</strong> Semester 2 has fewer units than Semester 1, but it's not the lighter half. Domain 2 alone carries more exam weight than Domain 1, and it only shows up in Units 7&ndash;10. Don't let a shorter unit count read as lower priority when you're pacing the year.
  </div>
</div>

## Help Along the Way

